# Only game/ is the site. This matters when Vercel's Root Directory is left as the
# repo root; with Root Directory set to `game` (see DEPLOY.md) it is redundant but
# harmless.
art-source
node_modules
tests
tools
test-results
playwright-report
game/drafts
game/qa

# SOURCE ART that has to stay in the repo because it is the input to a build, but has
# no business being uploaded. Each one is consumed by a tool and never fetched by the
# game:
#   assets/GIF/*.gif        -> tools/gif-to-grid.mjs   -> assets/char/*-gif.png
#   assets/char/*-gif.png   -> tools/slice-char.mjs    -> assets/char/mammoth-*.webp
#   assets/option-shape/*.png -> tools/build-option-shapes.mjs -> the .webp + the rings
#   assets/art/cover.png    -> tools/assets.mjs        -> assets/art/cover.webp
game/assets/GIF
game/assets/char/*-gif.png
game/assets/option-shape/*.png
game/assets/art/cover.png

# Entries for files that have since been DELETED are deliberately not kept here. A
# stale ignore line is not harmless: it reads as "this file exists and is excluded",
# so the next person looking for the shelf art or the unnamed panel dumps goes hunting
# for something that is only in git history. Removed in the same pass as the files:
#   assets/env/hang-stone.webp, assets/env/hs.webp   dead since the overhang became fog
#   assets/ui/icons/NORMAL-BUTTON.png, PRESSED-BUTTON.png, image.png
#   assets/art/image.png                              unidentified duplicate renders
#   assets/ui/icons/ChatGPT*.png                      now art-source/btn-play-*-raw.png
#   6 unused assets/option-shape/*.png alternates     no shape in the curriculum
